+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2FTMXD2S83CCJ9B0H279E2R","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T11:10:52Z","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:ID.AM.S5"],"title":"classification-conflict: 4 in onfinance-db-model-master","description":"Four classification-conflict gaps in db-models-mongodb: (1) db-models-mongodb.default.user.user_debank_url is declared as a URLField (a profile link), but a DeBank profile URL carries the user's crypto wallet address, which identifies the user's financial account and holdings; took the stricter class financial + spdi + pii. (2) db-models-mongodb.default.secrets: zerodha_username could be a plain login name (restricted) or the Zerodha client ID / UCC (pii), classified restricted + pii; apiSecrets and accessToken could be application secrets (restricted) or password-equivalent trading-account credentials (spdi under the SPDI Rules 2011 'passwords'), classified restricted + spdi + pii; apiKey stays restricted only as a Kite Connect app identifier. (3) db-models-mongodb.default.user.profile_answers is an untyped DynamicField that could be generic onboarding preferences (confidential) or the user's self-reported profile/risk answers (personal data); took the stricter class confidential + pii, pending a runtime sample by runtime-probe-datapipeline; the same untyped-structure conflict applies to user_binance_auth_creds and entity.fundamental_analysis/technical_analysis/important_links. (4) applications/db-models/env/dev.json declares dataClassification ['internal'], but the models this application ships define pii, spdi (user_password, zerodha_password, zerodha_2fa, trading-account tokens) and financial (portfolio holdings and values) fields; the stricter classes were taken in the catalog. The application README also calls the library 'SQLAlchemy models', while the code is mongoengine (MongoDB) documents.","methods":["refresh-metastore"],"subjects":[{"type":"repo","appId":"db-models","repoId":"onfinance-db-model-