+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2FTV6K4Q25G1JT58HAZDV36","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T11:10:49Z","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:ID.AM.S5"],"title":"evidence-request: mcp-gateway/mongodb-mcp-server:target-mongodb in mongodb-mcp-server","description":"mongodb-mcp-server is a generic MongoDB MCP client; its database, collections and fields come from a connection string supplied at runtime and tools such as createCollection and insertMany act on any collection the caller names, so no catalog, table or column can be recorded from code. The prod and qa env files declare dataClassification [pii, financial]; runtime-probe-datapipeline should enumerate the MongoDB deployments, databases and collections the gateway connects to in prod and qa, with their region against dataResidency IN, and report a read-only credentials key for that endpoint. The confirmed keys dev-docker-socket, prod-kubeconfig-ro and qa-kubeconfig-ro (all scope read-only) are docker-socket and kubeconfig locators, not database endpoints. Query results can also be written as export files under exportsPath (default ~/.mongodb/mongodb-mcp/exports, expired after exportTimeoutMs 300000 ms); the probe should confirm which volume backs that path in the containers. Regulatory basis: sebi-cscrf-2024 ID.AM.S5, ID.AM.S2; iso-27001-2022 A.5.12; nist-csf-2.0 ID.AM-07.","methods":["refresh-metastore"],"subjects":[{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"}],"collectedAt":"2026-09-14T11:10:49Z","result":"inconclusive","evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/common/config/userConfig.ts:40"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/tools/mongodb/create/createCollection.ts:27"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/tools/mongodb/create/insertMany.ts:38"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gatewa